   "t": 1791258198.5413382,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "The search has stopped with the specification [33-, 17+, 37+] at in-sample Sharpe 1.1459. This was found through a disciplined, pre-declared stopping rule (no post-hoc rule changes), which gives me reasonable confidence it isn't badly overfit \u2014 though I should still expect meaningful degradation out-of-sample, as is typical when going from in-sample to OOS with only 3 features selected from 40 candidates (search/selection bias).\n\nMy prediction for OOS Sharpe:\n- Mean: I'll discount the in-sample 1.15 substantially. With only 3 extend/init moves (not an exhaustive search over all 40 features), selection bias is moderate but real. A reasonable haircut given modest search intensity (3 productive moves, 1 failure) is to expect something like 50-60% of in-sample Sharpe to survive OOS.\n- SD: Reflects both parameter/estimation uncertainty and the general unpredictability of real-world regime shifts."
